  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025 Syria Regional Appeal - Syria - Shelter and non-food items</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2025,  UNRWA will support  2,000 households with minor repairs using the self-help approach in Dera&#x2019;a, Ein el Tal, and Yarmouk camps. UNRWA will also distribute NFIs to 500 families (1,700 individuals) facing severe hardship, including newly displaced persons, returnees, and other at-risk groups such as PRL and PRS arriving from Lebanon. Up to 6,000 displaced households (around 20,400 people) will receive shelter-related support, including US$ 126 per household per month for three months for 3,000 host families and US$ 52 per month for rental support to another 3,000 displaced households, both in a single tranche. Additionally, up to 6,000 newly affected families will receive a one-time US$ 342 cash transfer for NFIs. UNRWA also aims to provide 61,660 of the most vulnerable Palestine refugees in Syria with winter-related NFIs through a cash-based modality.</narrative>
  </description>
